From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:09:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10943/11362] Record that the ARC generalization floor check
 cannot fail

Milestone 609 has zero ARC tasks -- twelve tasks of SMT certification, convex
factor energy, certified selection and queue self-learning, none touching the
live ARC agent -- and arc_levelup_guarantee_lint reports three
generalization-testing-floor tasks detected.

Confirmed by running the predicate. Its ARC-scope guard is a bare substring
test, "arc" not in p, and "research" contains "arc". Every task prompt in this
repository says research, research_conductor or research-roadmap, so the scope
guard passes for every task that will ever be checked. One ordinary
machine-learning phrase, held-out, then completes the match. The three matched
tasks scoped in on the words research and research_conductor. None mentions ARC.

The check is therefore not miscalibrated, it is structurally incapable of
failing, in the guard protecting this project's stated north star, 59 days
before the submission deadline. It survived because WARN-only output looks
identical whether the floor is satisfied or unevaluable.

The fix is a word boundary on the scope test, and it is deliberately not made
here: applying it changes what the check says about past roadmaps, which is an
operator's call rather than a quiet edit during a status pass. The regression
test is obvious -- the current 609 roadmap must count zero.

This is the first bug class the QA-Layer Authenticity Discipline names,
occurring in a guard that discipline does not list in GUARD_TARGETS.

